  "problem": "If $A$ is false and $B$ is true, then $A\u21d4\u00acB$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P\u21d4Q$ is true if $P\u21d2Q$ **and** $Q\u21d2P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P\u21d4Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo, when $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A\u21d4\u00acB) & =(\\text{F}\u21d4\u00ac\\text{T}) \\\\  & =(\\text{F}\u21d4\\text{F}) \\\\  & =\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\u00acB\\,$ | $\\,A\u21d4\u00acB\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n|  |  |  |  |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
